Remanufacturing operations require detailed material knowledge enabling informed processing decisions. Hidden material composition creates risks of incompatible processing (corrosion from chemical cleaners, incompatible re-machining) damaging core value. Material passports enable remanufacturers to optimize processes for specific material combinations.

Embedded material information reduces uncertainty and enables fast decision-making. Hazardous substance documentation prevents worker exposure and contamination during processing. Material compatibility information optimizes remanufacturing economics by enabling specialized process selection.